{"kind":"report","text":"Ready for independent review at exact clean head e82d9fff2d858662f7e3ddc2492c6d5b559d46fa on request/ci-suite-dedup.\n\nThe head makes one uncached race-enabled go test -json ./... run authoritative in CI and feeds that same stream to the six-case reporter. Local make spike still runs only its 17 named tests when no captured stream is supplied. The preview-clone gate keeps the exact single-main ref, exact HEAD/branch, vet, ordinary build, and clean-checkout assertions but drops its identical test pass. The layout test keeps the public module declaration and tracked spike-result presence while removing compiled-path and finished-migration absence tripwires.\n\nRemoved executions and unique claims:\n- CI make test: no unique current claim. There are no race-conditioned Go files; the retained race run executes the same 19 packages/tests, while make build separately proves ordinary production compilation.\n- Standalone make spike: its 17 tests already run in the authoritative suite. Only six-case selection/rendering is unique, and that now consumes the same JSON.\n- Preview-clone make test: identical tracked bytes were already tested. Clone topology, vet, ordinary build, and cleanliness remain.\n- Retained make race-equivalent JSON run: uniquely checks exercised concurrency for data races.\n- Retained vet/build/UI/diff and preview topology gates keep their separate claims.\n\nMeasured locally: make test 221.19s; make race 189.21s; focused make spike 25.13s. The new authoritative uncached race+JSON run took 202.22s and captured-stream evidence regeneration took 0.24s with byte-identical tracked SPIKE-RESULTS.md. This removes two ordinary full-suite executions and the 25-second named rerun from the CI path; the 17 named cases fall from four executions to one.\n\nConditions met: make test passes; make race passes; go test -race -count=1 -json ./... passes; both local named and captured-stream make spike modes pass and leave the stable tracked evidence unchanged; make vet/build pass; the committed exact-head preview clone passes vet/build/topology/cleanliness; git diff --check passes; current-main merge-tree succeeds; worktree is clean.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers are CI/repository policy and the adversarial evidence application tooling; kernel, Nexus, Workroom interpreter/fold, projection contract, MCP/CLI runtime, and UI contracts are preserved. No architecture-page update is needed. Security: race coverage, static analysis, ordinary builds, exact clone topology, no-credential checkout, and all six adversarial cases remain. pipefail preserves the test producer's failure and tee prints/stores its JSON, while missing/skip/fail/malformed evidence remains fail-closed in the reporter. Simplification: one suite stream plus one projection is the smallest design; the no-input focused fallback keeps local evidence reproduction cheap without a second CI path.\n\nSeparate decision requested by #2920: the optional Gitea compose profile remains unexercised and uncertified. Remove spike/compose.yaml and spike/FORGE.md in separately governed work unless a ratifier chooses to fund an automated forge-certification lane; this head does not silently broaden scope by deleting them.","body":{"branch":"request/ci-suite-dedup","head":"e82d9fff2d858662f7e3ddc2492c6d5b559d46fa","status":"ready-for-review"}}